<title>FRANCE: Strikers disrupt air traffic in three French towns.</title>
<headline>Strikers disrupt air traffic in three French towns.</headline>
<dateline>NANTES 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial carriers were unable to take off or land in the French cities of Nantes and Brest on Thursday after strikers disrupted air traffic in three towns.</p>
<p>Air traffic in the town of Quimper in Brittany was nearly paralysed by the strikes called by regional chambers of industry and commerce opposed to plans to curtail wage increases.</p>
<p>Workers in the fire and security departments led the labour action at the airport in the western city of Nantes. Flights were re-routed to Saint-Nazaire and Rennes. Planes scheduled to land in Brest in Brittany were directed to Lorient.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
